<<Act Zoran zoranChill 0.25 0.2 #a20404>>
Zoran: Ah, delegation. The mark of a true ruler...
<<Act Zoran zoranTalk 0.25 0.2 #a20404>>
Zoran: ...Or at least, one who does not wish to micromanage every miserable little decision.

Zoran: Instead of selecting one town at a time like some peasant fumbling with a ledger.
Zoran: you can select multiple structures by simply <b>clicking and dragging</b> over the towers you want to select.

<<Act Zoran zoranSmug 0.25 0.2 #a20404>>
Zoran: But perhaps you are the meticulous type, unwilling to commit to a single sweeping motion.
<<Act Zoran zoranSurprise 0.25 0.2 #a20404>>
Zoran: Fine!
<<Act Zoran zoranTalk 0.25 0.2 #a20404>>
Zoran: You may also hold <sprite name="key_shift"> and add to your selection.

<<Act Zoran zoranSmug 0.25 0.2 #a20404>>
Zoran: [smoothWave]Now, onto something truly convenient![/smoothWave]
<<Act Zoran zoranChill 0.25 0.2 #a20404>>
Zoan: War is…
<<Act Zoran zoranTalk 0.25 0.2 #a20404>>
Zoran: tedious at best, and unsightly at worst.
Zoran: Your Majesty surely has more important matters to attend to than babysitting every little skirmish.
Zoran: Instead of constantly issuing attack orders...
Zoran: simply <b>double-click</b> when attacking an enemy encampment, and your troops will continue their assault without further supervision.
<<Act Zoran zoranChill 0.25 0.2 #a20404>>
Zoran: Now, try it!
Zoran: Select multiple structures, send your troops, and let them handle the dirty work while you…
<<Act Zoran zoranTalk 0.25 0.2 #a20404>>
Zoran: I don’t know…
<<Scene #000000 0.585>>
Zoran: sit on a throne or whatever it is monarchs do?

